   "fix": "Make both public at the natural level: `theorem map_internalEdges_of_le [Fintype E(G)] [Fintype E(H)] [DecidablePred (\u00b7 \u2208 E(H))] (h : H \u2264 G) (T : Finset V(H)) : (H.internalEdges T).map (Set.embeddingOfSubset _ _ h.edgeSet_mono) = (G.internalEdges (T.map (Set.embeddingOfSubset _ _ h.vertexSet_mono))).filter (\u00b7 .1 \u2208 E(H))`, and the same for `incidentEdges`. Derive the `restrict` and `deleteEdges` lemmas from these.",
   "issue": "`map_internalEdges_of_le` (and its twin `map_incidentEdges_of_le`, line 58) takes a vertex map `fV : V(G) \u21aa V(H)` with `hfV : (fV x).1 = x.1`. Since `H \u2264 G` gives `V(H) \u2286 V(G)`, such an `fV` exists only when the vertex sets are equal, so the extra parameters `fV`, `hfV`, `T`, `hT` are only ever filled with `refl`/`S`. The general subgraph result is also private and cannot be reused for vertex deletion or induced subgraphs.",
   "line": 33
